1
00:00:00,200 --> 00:00:04,700
When your business needs a new capability, build it as a connected app.

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:09,700
Its interface, data and behaviour become part of the same commerce environment.

3
00:00:10,200 --> 00:00:15,500
The visual designer and coding agent work on the same versioned app definition.

4
00:00:15,800 --> 00:00:21,700
Connect views and editable fields instead of maintaining a separate custom administration.

5
00:00:22,200 --> 00:00:27,500
Define app-owned records, relationships and the settings an installation needs.

6
00:00:27,800 --> 00:00:33,700
Shared storage keeps app data scoped without creating a database table for every installation.

7
00:00:34,200 --> 00:00:39,500
Connect app actions to native events and the existing Flow Builder.

8
00:00:39,800 --> 00:00:45,700
Follow execution history and reuse reviewed work in a repeatable flow.

9
00:00:46,200 --> 00:00:51,500
Use Veyndo AI, or bring Codex or Claude Code into the same app workflow.

10
00:00:51,800 --> 00:00:57,700
Agent and app operations remain subject to current shop permissions and review controls.

11
00:00:58,200 --> 00:01:04,200
Save immutable app versions and test installed behaviour in a private environment.

12
00:01:04,500 --> 00:01:08,000
Review what the package changes and what it is allowed to access.

13
00:01:08,300 --> 00:01:11,700
Publish deliberately, with version history available for subsequent changes.

14
00:01:12,200 --> 00:01:17,500
Apps extend the shop through shared commerce, permissions, events and releases.

15
00:01:17,800 --> 00:01:23,700
Explore App Studio and build your next connected capability.
